  "question": {
    "text": "For isothermal expansion of an ideal gas, the correct combination of the thermodynamic parameters will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gA0Dx",
      "text": "$\\Delta U=0, Q=0, W \\neq 0$ and $\\Delta H \\neq 0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "GVP4h",
      "text": "$\\Delta U \\neq 0, Q \\neq 0, W \\neq 0$ and $\\Delta H=0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "oWngq",
      "text": "$\\Delta U=0, Q \\neq 0, W=0$ and $\\Delta H \\neq 0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "GqPRV",
      "text": "$\\Delta U=0, Q \\neq 0, W \\neq 0$ and $\\Delta H=0$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For isothermal expansion of an ideal gas\r\n$$\r\n\\Delta T=0\r\n$$\r\n$\\therefore$ From $\\Delta U=n C_{v} \\Delta T$\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\\Delta U=0 \\text { and, from } \\\\\r\n\\Delta H=n C_{\\rho} \\Delta t=0\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$\r\nFrom first law of thermodynamics,\r\n$$\r\n\\Delta U=Q+W\r\n$$\r\nas\r\n$$\r\n\\Delta U=0 \\Rightarrow Q \\neq 0\r\n$$\r\nand\r\n$$\r\nW \\neq 0\r\n$$\r\n$\\therefore$ Parameters are\r\n$$\r\n\\Delta U=0, Q \\neq 0 ; W \\neq 0\r\n$$\r\nand $\\Delta H=0$",
    "image": null
  },
